# Build context for `gcloud run deploy --source .`. Everything here is excluded
# from the image AND from the tarball uploaded to Cloud Build, so this file is
# both a security control and a deploy-time cost control.

# ── Secrets. Never in an image layer. ────────────────────────────────────────
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this the live TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET are baked into a layer that anyone with pull access to
# Artifact Registry can read. They are already injected at runtime by
# --set-env-vars in .github/workflows/deploy.yml, so shipping them in the image
# is pure downside.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*-key.json
service-account*.json
*.pem
*.p12

# ── Version control and local envs ───────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
.uv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Node / Next build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
console/node_modules/
console/.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Large working data the API does not read at runtime ──────────────────────
# api/geo.py DOES read console/public/data/districts.geojson, so console/public
# must stay in the context. These do not.
data/raw/
data/interim/
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.zip

# ── The launch film. 5.9 GB of PNG frames and MP4s that the API never reads. ─
# Without this line every deploy uploads them to Cloud Build and bakes them into
# the image: a slow, expensive build and a needlessly enormous container.
video/out/
video/assets/

# ── Docs, screenshots, tests — not needed to serve a request ─────────────────
docs/screenshots/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
uv.lock
